(d) Married individuals filing separate returns

There is hereby imposed on the taxable income of every married individual (as defined in section 7703) who does not make a single return jointly with his spouse, a tax determined in accordance with the following:


<!-- rtdf-block-id: sara/section1:b0024; role: provision; provision-id: sara/section1(d); source-lines: 39-41; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
declaration subsection_d_applies content boolean
  depends on world content W.World,
             taxpayer content W.Entity,
             taxable_year content integer,
             spouses content list of W.Entity
  equals
    exists sp among spouses such that
      not (exists jr among (W.joint_return_event_values of world) such that
             jr.agents contains taxpayer and jr.agents contains sp
             and (W.optional_date_equals of jr.starts, (W.first_day_year of taxable_year))
             and (W.optional_date_equals of jr.ends, (W.last_day_year of taxable_year)))

scope Tax:
  definition holds_d equals
    subsection_d_applies of world, taxpayer, taxable_year, spouses

declaration schedule_d content list of Bracket equals
  [bracket_d_1; bracket_d_2; bracket_d_3; bracket_d_4; bracket_d_5]
```

    (i) 15% of taxable income if the taxable income is not over $18,450;

